  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forging a Greener Peace in the Hirshabelle State of Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will concentrate on territory recently recovered from al-Shabaab (AS) by the Somali government in Hirshabelle State. Establishing natural resource management mechanisms and restoring sustainable agricultural value chains demands an approach that integrates rural and urban engagement via meaningful socioeconomic networks. The project aims to bolster stability in newly recovered areas by harnessing &#x2018;anchor towns&#x2019; &#x2013; urban and peri-urban areas under government control &#x2013; targeting the most critical demographic stressors while strengthening and extending informal and formal local institutions into the fragile periphery, where AS influence remains strong.</narrative>
  </description>
